# Narrow on purpose: only file types whose LINE ENDINGS CHANGE BEHAVIOUR are
# pinned here, so this file causes no repo-wide renormalisation. Everything
# else keeps following each machine's core.autocrlf.
#
# *.mjs -- scripts/{check-linked-project,load-hardware-catalog,
#          purge-legacy-documents}.mjs start with `#!/usr/bin/env node`. On a
#          Windows checkout with autocrlf the shebang line ended in \r, and
#          vitest's transform rejected the file outright ("SyntaxError:
#          Invalid or unexpected token", naming no test), so both
#          purge-legacy-documents test files failed to LOAD.
# *.sql -- migrations are applied byte-for-byte and compared by hash (the
#          13 Oct 2026 accidental dev push was audited that way); CRLF in a
#          dollar-quoted function body is stored into the function.
# *.sh  -- a CRLF shell script fails on its first line under bash.
#
# The index already held all of these as LF, so adding this changed no
# committed content -- only what a Windows working copy looks like.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf
